# The origin of the HTTPS CDN (task 107, ADR 0071, docs/ops/cdn.md): the CDN
# resource pulls the ciphertext of large files under this name from bff's
# origin listener (Cdn.Origin of bff.yaml, port 20480 on teamgram_net only,
# never published on the host). bff refuses every request without the right
# X-Pluma-Origin-Auth, which the CDN resource adds, before it reads the path;
# Caddy passes the header, the Range and the conditional headers on as they
# came, and the 206 back as bff sent it.
#
# The Caddyfile imports this file only when PLUMA_CDN_ORIGIN_DOMAIN is set
# (docker-compose.web.yaml): a site with an empty address would stop the
# whole Caddyfile. The certificate is Let's Encrypt's, as for the other names.
#
# - No encode, and no Accept-Encoding to bff: the answers are byte ranges of
#   ciphertext, which neither compresses nor may change.
# - Neither Server nor Via in the answers, Caddy's own errors (502 while bff
#   is down) included.
# - No log directive, so no access log: the header, the token of the query
#   and the ids of files in the paths are never written. bff logs the
#   origin's requests without them.
{$PLUMA_CDN_ORIGIN_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy bff:20480 {
		header_up -Accept-Encoding
	}
	header {
		-Server
		-Via
	}
	handle_errors {
		header -Server
	}
}
